# Git workflow

When starting work on a **new feature**, always use a **new branch**. Do not implement features directly on `main`.

## Before coding

1. Confirm you are not on `main` (or switch/create a branch).
2. Create a branch from an up-to-date `main`, e.g. `feature/login`, `feature/dashboard`, `feature/spending`.
3. Keep the branch focused on one slice of work.

## When done

Merge to `main` only when that slice works and is ready to integrate.

This matches `PLAN.md` — feature branches are the default workflow for this repo.

## Commits

- Plain commit messages only (title + optional body).
- **Never** add `Co-authored-by:` trailers — including `Co-authored-by: Cursor` or any agent attribution.
- Do not mention Cursor, agents, or AI in commit messages unless the user explicitly asks.
